+# Performance history
+
+## SessionStart health gate
+
+The health-gate change moved `PRAGMA quick_check` off the `SessionStart` read
+path. The same change added the trigger-maintained `meta.fts_rows` counter and
+the `CHECK (length(body) <= 2000)` constraint.
+
+On a synthetic store with 5,000 records and 15,000 cues, the end-to-end
+`SessionStart` hook p50 was:
+
+| Configuration | p50 |
+| --- | ---: |
+| Before: live `quick_check` on the read path | Measured result not found in this checkout or its Git history. |
+| After: recorded `quick_check` result and `fts_rows` counter | 1.030292 ms |
+
+The after value was measured on 2026-09-14 with 300 invocations of the release
+binary using `muninn-bench perf --records 5000 --cues 15000 --runs 300`. It is
+an end-to-end subprocess measurement (process start through exit), not an
+estimate. The standalone 9.6 ms `quick_check` observation in the source is not
+used as a substitute for the missing before-hook measurement.
